WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.330
I'm Megumi Seki from Kamoshika Fermentation.

2
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:08.170
Thank you for joining today's class on using green ume.

3
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:13.050
Do you all have your one kilo of green ume ready?

4
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:17.570
We're going to use all of it today.

5
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.570
It's like putting a lid on it with sugar.

6
00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:26.270
All done.

7
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.250
And that's the preparation finished.

8
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.130
So it goes "pshh," and bubbles up with a gurgle.

9
00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:40.170
This is the normal state.

10
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.730
When you stir with clean hands,

11
00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:48.770
the fermentation gets pushed along, and the ume slowly float up.

12
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.010
When it's ready to drink, you drink this extract.

13
00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:59.290
the inside looks like this. Pretty, isn't it?

14
00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.310
It looks like this.

15
00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:06.770
so I hope you'll try making ume in June.

16
00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.390
Bringing fermented food back into the kitchen

17
00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:15.730
and letting it quietly support your everyday life in a simple way,

18
00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:20.210
that is what fermented food is. I hope we can keep making it together.

19
00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.650
Thank you so much for joining this class today.

